'' The same refusal with -target BEFORE -m32, because the width override is resolved
'' after the whole line is read and must not depend on the order. linux-x86_64 has no
'' 32-bit member -- Linux is 64-bit only by decision (docs D14) -- so -m32 is refused
'' rather than ignored. Until 2026-11-08 every target refused it; TARGET_WIN32 made the
'' refusal a matter of the family, and the message says which family it names.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -m32 -target linux-x86_64 tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: TKO0104: 32-bit targets are supported on Windows only; 'linux-x86_64' has no 32-bit member
